# Skills guide

Skills are `SKILL.md` files with YAML frontmatter, loaded as slash commands. The **directory name** under `skills/<domain>/` is the command name.

Canonical authoring rules: `rules/dev/skill-quality-standards.md`. Canonical frontmatter schema: `core/schemas/skill-frontmatter.json`. Do not restate the field list here — read the schema; a copied list drifts.

## Adding a skill

1. Create `skills/<domain>/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` with `skill-creator` — never hand-write one
2. `python3 scripts/validate-skill-frontmatter.py skills/<domain>/<skill-name>/SKILL.md`
3. Update the skill table and any documented count in `README.md`
4. `make validate` (`check-doc-claims` fails on a stale count)

## Portability

One `skills/` tree ships to every target. Keep skill bodies provider-neutral: check `core/capabilities/platforms.json` before relying on subagents, hooks, a statusline, or background tasks, and degrade explicitly when a capability is absent — a stated fallback, or a plain "unsupported here". Never silently pretend it worked.

**User guide:** [docs/user/agent-kit.md](../../docs/user/agent-kit.md) — agent-kit distribution repos (`repo-scaffold --type plugin`).
